/**
 * The Great American Road Trip -- 10-episode conversation series for Memoria
 * Three generations drive an old minivan ("Bessie") from New Jersey to California
 * so 78-year-old Grandpa Walt -- who refuses to fly -- can finally see the Pacific
 * Ocean. Over ten days and ten stops the trip goes progressively wrong (breakdowns,
 * tourist traps, a desert meltdown) and somehow turns into the best thing the family
 * has ever done.
 * 6 core characters: Walt (78M grandpa, refuses to fly, paper maps, wants to see the
 *   ocean), Roy (49M dad, driving, budget-obsessed, dad jokes), Lori (46F mom, the
 *   planner and referee), Paige (16F, secretly filming a documentary on her phone),
 *   Sam (11M, collects rocks, names the van, "are we there yet"), Rhonda (52F, a solo
 *   biker they keep crossing paths with across the country).
 * Plus rotating local guests: Flo (diner waitress), Ranger Kim (Yellowstone),
 *   Duke (desert tow-truck driver), Bud (roadside-attraction owner).
 * The 10 "days" are 10 actual days of the cross-country drive.
 * Speech patterns: NO g-dropping (full -ing forms), contractions OK,
 *   fillers, hedges, false starts, road-trip chaos and family bickering.
 * Format: ~16 lines per day per language.
 */

